UNESCO LANGUAGE PRESERVATION FUND – GRANT APPLICATION

Project Title: National Languages Bill – Zambia Indigenous Language Integration

Applicant: Major Dr. Kabanga Allan

Project Description:
This proposal seeks UNESCO support for the implementation of Zambia’s National Languages Bill, formally inducting Bemba and Lozi as official languages. This aligns with the UNESCO 2019–2028 International Decade of Indigenous Languages.

Requested Funding: $350,000

Project Duration: 2025–2028

Key Activities:
- National translation program development
- Teacher training and curriculum localization
- Media content production in Bemba and Lozi
- Traditional leader integration and civic outreach

Partnerships: Zambia Ministry of Education, Barotse Royal Establishment, House of Chiefs

